A Interface defines a structure or a contract that an object should follow 
=> An interface tells us what properties and Methods an object should have, but it doesn't generally define 
   how those methods work 


   interface NameOfInterface{
    variable1: dataType;
    variable2: dataType;
    variable3:dataType;
    .
    .
    .
    variablen: dataType;
    methods(); returnType;

   }

